# Shared by every hy4-<bpw> profile (sourced from it after QSE_HY4_BPW, the weights' repository, revision and size
# and the memory need are set): Tencent's Hy4-flash (engine/models/hy4_flash) in one of our EXL3 packs. The pack
# holds its DFly2 draft layers and its four Engram tables, so nothing else is fetched (QSE_ASSETS empty). Text only:
# the vision tower in the pack is not served yet. QSE_ENGINE_FLAGS replaces the 27B's model and drafter flags in
# ops/start.sh; the rest of serve.env (port, ledger, conductor, limits, caches) is shared.
QSE_WEIGHTS=hy4-${QSE_HY4_BPW}
QSE_WEIGHTS_DIR=${HOME}/models/hy4-flash-exl3-${QSE_HY4_BPW}
QSE_WEIGHTS_FILES=
# what weights_ok checks beside the index's shards: the four Engram tables are not in the index. Both packs carry
# the same four files, so a second pack under ${HOME}/models links them from the first (ops/fetch_weights.py share)
QSE_WEIGHTS_ALSO="engram.layers.1.safetensors engram.layers.11.safetensors engram.layers.21.safetensors engram.layers.31.safetensors"
QSE_ASSETS=
unset QWEN38_EXL3 QWEN38_DRAFT_EXL3 QWEN38_DRAFT_HEAD_EXL3
# any drafter but none drafts with the pack's DFly2 layers and the lookup, cut by StairCut over the pack's price
# file (ops/prices/hy4-flash/<profile>.dgx-spark.json, frozen by QWEN38_HY4_DRAFT_FREEZE); the drafted text equals
# the plain text
QSE_ENGINE_FLAGS="--model ${QSE_WEIGHTS_DIR} --drafter mtp"
# thinking: a request with no effort, where no client, no conductor plan and no --think-budget decided, thinks in the
# template's high mode at the family's own default level, medium (8,192 tokens and the answer reserve; the spec in
# engine/models/hy4_flash/arch.py, ENG-468). serve.env's REASONING_EFFORT keeps one job here: off turns thinking off
VISION=off
# served and fit-tested at 262,144 tokens; the state is 16,896 bytes a token, 4.13 GiB at this window. The
# checkpoint reads 1,048,576; past 262,144 is not tested
MAX_LEN=262144
# ENG-485: side slots as every lane family's, serve.env's lanes (QSE_PARALLEL), each the full MAX_LEN on the shared
# KV pool (QSE_KV_POOL on, QSE_SIDE_MAX_LEN 0): a lane's latents and indexer keys take pages only for the rows it
# holds, and an idle conversation goes to the park and the NVMe spill under pressure. The lanes take turns (no
# joint pass). Written out as _flashnext.env does, the values serve.env has
QSE_PARALLEL=8
QSE_KV_POOL=on
# The round runner without its pipe: with the pipe the drafter accepts fewer tokens a round on this family (one client,
# a 3,000-token prompt, 600 out, hy4-3.56: 2.965 against 3.169 on one lane, decode 33.06 and 33.43 tok/s against
# 35.40, -5.6 to -6.6 %); without it 3.169 and 35.00 tok/s (-1.1 %). The text is the same either way
QSE_RUNNER_PIPE=0
# ENG-609: the engine's CUDA allocator on expandable segments, Flash-Next's setting (SPD-257, _flashnext.env; ops/start.sh
# hands it to the engine's command only). Without it the reserve fragments while what is allocated stays flat
# (hy4-3.56, 8 lanes, release 0.17.0, 2026-11-24): a cold 250,016-token raw prompt on side slot 5 took the reserve
# from 76.4 to 89.35 GiB by row 118,784 with 75.19 allocated at most, and MemAvailable to 10.39 GiB. With it, on the
# same release, a cold 129,951-token prompt on that slot, two other requests in flight, held the reserve at or under
# 77.80 GiB (MemAvailable 21.82 at least); on this tree, at a peak of 82, a cold 249,971-token prompt on slot 0
# held the engine's reserve at or under 78.09 (the decision models' pools aside). Captures run on plain segments through
# engine/capture_lock.py, as Flash-Next's. Unsupported (the load line says how many segments are expandable):
# max_split_size_mb:512
QSE_ENGINE_ALLOC_CONF=${QSE_ENGINE_ALLOC_CONF-expandable_segments:True}
# the Engram tables (38.11 GiB) are read past the page cache through a 2 GiB hot-row cache
QWEN38_HY4_TABLE=cold
QWEN38_HY4_TABLE_CACHE_GB=2
QSE_PAGE_CACHE_DROP=${QSE_WEIGHTS_DIR}
# the lookup's suffix store of this tokenizer (the other models' stores hold other token ids, and the server
# refuses them by fingerprint)
QWEN38_SUFFIX_STORE=${HOME}/.qwen38-spark-engine/suffix-hy4
# a folder of the disk tier's own a pack
QSE_DISK_CACHE=${HOME}/.qwen38-spark-engine/cache/disk-hy4-${QSE_HY4_BPW}
# MEM_CEILING_GIB and MEM_PEAK_GIB: each pack's profile sets them (hy4-<bpw>.env), as every family's (OPS-308; until
# then the model set its own from what its load held, and the limits moved three times in two days)
